 "_about": "Profile rig (v2), every body piece from zeus_exploded. Which piece hangs from which attachment point of its parent (index into the parent's attach list, top→bottom then left→right; 'pivot' = the parent's own pivot). offset: a nudge in parent px. Facing right: N = near side (in front), F = far side (behind, darkened copies). The thighs start at the hip joint under the skirt; the skirt (z 5) covers their tops. Layering: the near arm (z 10) is drawn over the head, because in profile it is closer to the camera than the beard; the far arm hangs further forward so the torso hides most of it. A socket can carry a third item, an [x,y] nudge in the piece's px (the feet: from the old cap under the sandal up to the bottom of the sole). Legs have an ankle: the leg IK aims at the ankle, and the foot (footN/footF) turns to stay flat; soles: leg → [foot bone, sole socket].",
